 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for delivery.** Committed revisions are pushed to connected browsers over WebSocket sessions managed by the delivery component. See [`docs/decisions/realtime-delivery.md`](decisions/realtime-delivery.md) for the analysis of polling, hosted services, and self-hosted WebSockets against latency, cost structure, and operational burden.
